- If using email: password-protect the PDF (or encrypt the message). Send the password via a different channel (phone or SMS).
- Use encrypted email (S/MIME or PGP) if available.
- Confirm how long they will keep the file and whether they’ll securely delete it once processed.

Extra checks before sending
- Open the file you plan to send and try selecting/copying the redacted area—if you can select the text, redaction isn’t complete.
- Check PDF properties/metadata and remove any sensitive metadata.
- Keep a record of who you sent it to and why; delete local copies if no longer needed.

