Short answer
- If the form only asks for the last four digits, send only the last four (e.g., XXX‑XX‑3456).
- If the form requires the full SSN, do NOT send it over regular email or an unsecured scan. Use a secure portal or an encrypted/transferred method (details below).

What to redact when scanning
- Redact the full SSN except for the digits the recipient explicitly asked for. If they asked for only the last four, mask the rest.
- Also remove SSN from the file name, the email subject, and any document metadata.

How to redact correctly (digital)
- Use a true redaction tool (Adobe Acrobat Pro’s Redact, or another PDF redaction feature). Proper redaction permanently removes the underlying text and metadata.
