How to redact correctly (paper)
- Permanently black out the SSN with an opaque permanent marker, then photocopy the redacted page and send the photocopy (the original with the marker can sometimes still reveal text if held up to light).
- Alternatively, cut out the digits and photocopy the result; keep or shred the original per security needs.

Secure ways to send a full SSN (if the recipient requires it)
- Upload via the organization’s secure portal (preferred).
- Encrypted email (S/MIME or PGP) if both parties support it.
- Password-protected PDF (use strong password) and send the password separately — e.g., via phone or SMS to a different number.
- Secure file-transfer services (SFTP, secure corporate file share) approved by the recipient.
- Fax only if the recipient confirms a monitored, secure fax line (fax is not ideal but sometimes used).

Other precautions
- Don’t include SSN in subject lines or filenames.
- Remove document metadata (author, hidden text) before sending.
- Limit other identifying data in the document (DOB, driver’s license, etc.) unless required.
- If in doubt, contact the organization and ask which secure method they prefer.

