Short answer: Yes — unless the requester explicitly needs the full SSN and provides a secure way to submit it, you should redact everything except the last four digits. Before sending any scan with an SSN, verify the recipient and use a secure channel.

Quick checklist
- Ask whether the full SSN is actually required; often the last 4 digits are sufficient. (You gave the last four as 3456.)
- If full SSN is not required, redact the first five digits and only include the last four.
- If the full SSN is required, insist on a secure delivery method (secure upload portal, encrypted email, password‑protected PDF) and confirm the recipient’s identity.
- Never put SSNs in subject lines or filenames.
- Remove metadata and ensure the redaction is permanent (flatten the file).
- Share any password via a separate channel (phone call or SMS), not in the same email.

How to redact correctly (so it can’t be recovered)
1. Use a proper redaction tool when available
   - Adobe Acrobat Pro: Use Redact tool → mark text → Apply Redactions → Save As.
2. If you don’t have Acrobat, edit the image/PDF and flatten
   - Mac Preview: Use the markup rectangle (fill black) to cover digits → File > Export as PDF, then Print → Save as PDF to flatten annotations.
   - Windows: Open image in Paint or Paint 3D, draw a solid black box, save, then print to PDF to flatten.
   - Mobile: Use markup to cover digits, then “Save as PDF” or export and flatten. Confirm the app actually burns the black box into the image (don’t rely on a temporary overlay).
3. Verify the redaction
   - Open the final file and try to select/copy the redacted area; if text can still be selected or the original can be seen if you change colors/brightness, the redaction is not permanent.
   - Check file metadata and remove it (PDF editors or “Save as” often help).

Secure sending options
- Secure upload portal provided by the organization (preferred).
- Encrypted email (S/MIME or PGP) or office secure messaging.
- Password‑protected PDF (use a strong password); do NOT send the password in the same email — share it by phone or separate channel.
- Fax or in-person drop-off if available.
- Avoid plain email or unsecured attachments whenever possible.

Sample message to ask the requester (you can send this)
"Hi — for the form you requested, do you need my full SSN or are the last four digits (3456) sufficient? If you require the full SSN, please provide a secure upload link or confirm you accept a password‑protected PDF; I will send the password on a separate channel. Thanks."

