- Try to select/search the redacted area in the final file — if the digits can be selected or found by text search/OCR, redaction failed.  
- Open the file in a text editor (for PDFs, sometimes text remains) or run a quick OCR check to be sure the numbers aren’t recoverable.

4) Metadata and filenames
- Remove personal data from file metadata (e.g., image EXIF). On Windows: File → Properties → Remove Personal Info. On Mac: export without location data.  
- Don’t include SSN in the filename or in the email subject/body.

5) Safer delivery options
- Use the organization’s secure upload portal whenever possible.  
- If you must send a file: encrypt the PDF (password-protect) and send the password by a different channel (phone or SMS).  
- Use secure email or an encrypted file-sharing service. Standard email is often only TLS in transit and could be stored unencrypted on mail servers.

6) If you’re unsure
- Ask the recipient: “Do you require the full SSN? If so, what secure upload/encryption method should I use?”  
- If they don’t provide a secure method, offer only the last four digits or call to provide the full number verbally.

