A clear checklist and safe ways to redact/submit:

1) Confirm need and recipient security
- Ask the requester why they need the full SSN and whether the last four digits will suffice.
- Ask for a secure method (organization upload portal, encrypted email or secure file transfer). If they don’t offer one, don’t send the full SSN by plain email or SMS.

2) If you can send only the last 4 digits
- Mask the rest (e.g., XXX-XX-3456) on the document and in the filename/subject.
- This is the safest option for most forms where identity verification is needed but full SSN is not required.

3) If you must send the full SSN, use one of these secure methods
- Secure upload portal provided by the organization (preferred).
- Encrypted email (S/MIME or PGP) or password‑protected PDF (AES encryption). Send the password by a different channel (phone or SMS).
- Secure file transfer (SFTP, secure company portal).

4) How to redact properly (don’t just hide or white-out in a way that can be reversed)
- Best: use a proper redaction tool (Adobe Acrobat’s Redact feature, or other PDF editors) that removes the text from the file — not just visually covers it.
  Steps in Acrobat: Tools → Redact → Mark for Redaction (select SSN) → Apply Redactions → Save As a new file. Then check by searching the PDF for the digits.
- macOS Preview workaround: draw a black rectangle over the number, then export as PDF and flatten by printing to PDF. Still test by searching the PDF for the number — if it’s removed, it’s good.
- If you redact on paper: permanently black marker the numbers, then scan the redacted paper. Do not simply cover them with a sticky note or use removable tape. If possible, cut out the numbers before scanning.
- After redaction, remove metadata/hidden text and disable OCR or ensure the OCR layer doesn’t contain the SSN. Test by opening the file and searching for the digits.

5) File naming and message
- Don’t put the SSN in the file name, email subject, or message body.
- Use a neutral filename (e.g., ID_document_redacted.pdf).
- If sending a password-protected PDF, send the password in a separate channel.

6) After sending
- Ask recipient to confirm secure receipt and their retention/deletion policy.
- Shred physical copies you no longer need and securely delete unnecessary digital copies.

Notes and a small clarification
- You wrote two different values (“000-00-0123” and “last four: 3456”). Which is the correct last-four? When you redact, use the correct digits so they match your form and ID.

