When to redact
- If the form or recipient only needs the last four digits, give only the last four.
- If an employer/agency explicitly requires the full SSN, ask for a secure upload method (encrypted portal or secure file transfer) rather than plain email/attachments.

How to redact safely (options)
1. If you have a paper copy
  - Physically black out the SSN with a permanent marker (not just a removable sticker).
  - Make a photocopy or scan the redacted paper. Do not scan first and then black out the digital copy (that can sometimes be reversible).
  - Verify the resulting scanned file does not show the redacted digits under different viewers or via image adjustments.

2. If you have a digital file (PDF/image)
  - Use a true redaction tool (e.g., Adobe Acrobat Pro “Redact” feature) that removes the text and underlying data permanently. Do not just draw a black box over the text in a PDF — that can be undone or the text may remain searchable.
