  - Remove metadata (Document Properties) and save as a new file name.

Protect the file in transit
- Best: use the recipient’s secure upload portal.
- If you must email: compress into a password-protected ZIP or password-protected PDF (use strong password) and send the password via a separate channel (text or phone).
- Consider using an encrypted file transfer service (e.g., Box, Dropbox with link protection, ShareFile) if available.

Verify recipient and necessity
- Confirm the recipient’s email and that they actually need the SSN. Ask if they accept last-four only or a secure upload.
- Keep a record of who you sent it to and why.

Quick checklist before sending
- Do they need the full SSN? If not, provide only last four.
- If sending full SSN, did they provide a secure channel? If not, ask for one.
- Did you use true redaction (not just drawing over text)?
- Did you remove metadata and any hidden text/OCR?
- Did you protect the file in transit (password or secure portal)?
- Did you avoid including the SSN in the email body or subject?

