2) Redaction rules
- If only last four are required: mask the first five digits (example format: XXX-XX-3456 or ***-**-3456).
- If you must send a document that contains the full SSN but only part should be visible, redact the parts that are not required before sending.

3) How to redact safely
- Physical redaction (before scanning): use a thick black permanent marker over the digits, then photocopy the redacted document and scan the photocopy. This prevents recovery of the underlying text.
- Electronic redaction (recommended for digital files): use a proper PDF redaction tool (e.g., Adobe Acrobat Pro: Tools → Redact → Mark for Redaction → Apply). After applying redaction, save a new file and verify the redacted text is not selectable or recoverable.
- Do NOT just draw a black box in a PDF viewer or image editor without using a redact feature — that can leave the underlying text intact and recoverable.
- If you convert a scanned image to PDF, flatten the PDF (or save it as a new image-based PDF) so no text layers remain.
- Remove metadata (PDF properties, EXIF data) after editing.

4) Sending securely
- Preferred: upload via the requester’s secure portal or encrypted file transfer (SFTP, secure web form).
- If you must email: encrypt the message (S/MIME or PGP) or send a password‑protected PDF (use a strong password) and share the password by a different channel (phone or SMS).
- Never put SSN in the email subject line or file name.
- Use services that support expiring links and require a password if using cloud storage.

5) Additional precautions
- Keep copies of what you sent and a record of why it was required.
- Limit distribution — send only to the person/department that needs it.
- Ask the recipient to confirm secure deletion after they’ve processed the document if appropriate.
- If the document will be stored, confirm how long and how it will be protected.

6) Quick checklist before sending
- [ ] Confirm they need full SSN (if not, supply last 4 only)
- [ ] Redact appropriately (physical or electronic redaction)
- [ ] Remove metadata / flatten PDF
- [ ] Use secure upload or encrypted email / password-protected PDF
